INT. ROOFTOP GREENHOUSE - AFTERNOON

Glass panes fogged with humidity. Rows of orchids. A watering can.

CASPIAN ODUYA, 40s, sorts seed packets at a potting bench. VERONIKA STANISLAWSKI, 50s, sits on an upturned crate, sipping tea. JUNE PAPADOPOULOS, 20s, leans on a shelf, headphones around her neck.

CASPIAN
The vault is on the third floor. The elevator needs a keycard. The stairwell has a camera.

VERONIKA
And the roof?

CASPIAN
Roof door is alarmed. But the greenhouse vent connects to the same shaft.

JUNE
How wide is the vent?

CASPIAN
Twenty inches.

JUNE
That's tight.

CASPIAN
You're small.

JUNE
I'm average.

VERONIKA
You're small, June. Be proud.

JUNE
I'm proud. I'm also claustrophobic.

CASPIAN
Veronika can talk you through.

VERONIKA
I'll hum.

JUNE
You'll hum?

VERONIKA
Whale songs. They help.

CASPIAN
We go Thursday. The night guard changes at ten.

VERONIKA
What about the dog?

CASPIAN
There's no dog.

VERONIKA
There was a dog last month.

CASPIAN
That was a different building.

JUNE
Can we confirm the dog?

CASPIAN
I'll confirm the dog.

VERONIKA
Good.

JUNE
Good.

They sit. A drip falls from a leaf. Veronika stirs her tea. June drums on her knee. Caspian sets down the seed packet.

CASPIAN
Anyone want a tomato?

VERONIKA
Is it a good one?

CASPIAN
Best on the roof.

JUNE
Obviously. It's the only one.

CASPIAN
(handing her one)
Eat.
